 ### [Mask Projection Culling](6836-mask-projection-culling.md)
-Mask Projection Culling is a visibility optimization technique that filters mesh vertices and faces by projecting them into multiple camera views and checking if they fall within dilated binary masks, removing geometry not visible in any view. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Face Coverage Mask Culling](3397-face-coverage-mask-culling.md) by operating in screen space using pre-computed or rendered masks rather than volumetric occupancy checks, and from [Voxel Backface Culling and Internal Face Masking](4569-voxel-backface-culling-and-internal-face-masking.md) by relying on multi-view consistency rather than local geometric orientation.
